    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 265 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `displayName` field is now computed and returned in owner responses, formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo changes, both leveraging the existing OpenAPI-generated DTO + MapStruct mapping so the field appears wherever an `Owner` is serialized (create and get):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` (generated at build) now carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nThe new `Cp06Tests.coreDisplayName` passes (creates an owner, then asserts `$.displayName` == `\"LastName, John\"`), and all 265 tests remain green. No changes to the OfficeFloor function pipeline were needed since the responder already maps through `OwnerMapper`.",
